\pard\plain \s40\li0\widctlpar\adjustright \shading1000\cbpat8 \f2\fs16\cgrid 00001 {\cf20 // dear imgui: Renderer Backend for modern OpenGL with shaders / programmatic pipeline}\par
00002 {\cf20 // - Desktop GL: 2.x 3.x 4.x}\par
00003 {\cf20 // - Embedded GL: ES 2.0 (WebGL 1.0), ES 3.0 (WebGL 2.0)}\par
00004 {\cf20 // This needs to be used along with a Platform Backend (e.g. GLFW, SDL, Win32, custom..)}\par
00005 \par
00006 {\cf20 // Implemented features:}\par
00007 {\cf20 //  [X] Renderer: User texture binding. Use 'GLuint' OpenGL texture identifier as void*/ImTextureID. Read the FAQ about ImTextureID!}\par
00008 {\cf20 //  [X] Renderer: Large meshes support (64k+ vertices) with 16-bit indices (Desktop OpenGL only).}\par
00009 {\cf20 //  [X] Renderer: Multi-viewport support (multiple windows). Enable with 'io.ConfigFlags |= ImGuiConfigFlags_ViewportsEnable'.}\par
00010 \par
00011 {\cf20 // About WebGL/ES:}\par
00012 {\cf20 // - You need to '#define IMGUI_IMPL_OPENGL_ES2' or '#define IMGUI_IMPL_OPENGL_ES3' to use WebGL or OpenGL ES.}\par
00013 {\cf20 // - This is done automatically on iOS, Android and Emscripten targets.}\par
00014 {\cf20 // - For other targets, the define needs to be visible from the imgui_impl_opengl3.cpp compilation unit. If unsure, define globally or in imconfig.h.}\par
00015 \par
00016 {\cf20 // You can use unmodified imgui_impl_* files in your project. See examples/ folder for examples of using this.}\par
00017 {\cf20 // Prefer including the entire imgui/ repository into your project (either as a copy or as a submodule), and only build the backends you need.}\par
00018 {\cf20 // Learn about Dear ImGui:}\par
00019 {\cf20 // - FAQ                  https://dearimgui.com/faq}\par
00020 {\cf20 // - Getting Started      https://dearimgui.com/getting-started}\par
00021 {\cf20 // - Documentation        https://dearimgui.com/docs (same as your local docs/ folder).}\par
00022 {\cf20 // - Introduction, links and more at the top of imgui.cpp}\par
00023 \par
00024 {\cf20 // CHANGELOG}\par
00025 {\cf20 // (minor and older changes stripped away, please see git history for details)}\par
00026 {\cf20 //  2024-XX-XX: Platform: Added support for multiple windows via the ImGuiPlatformIO interface.}\par
00027 {\cf20 //  2024-06-28: OpenGL: ImGui_ImplOpenGL3_NewFrame() recreates font texture if it has been destroyed by ImGui_ImplOpenGL3_DestroyFontsTexture(). (#7748)}\par
00028 {\cf20 //  2024-05-07: OpenGL: Update loader for Linux to support EGL/GLVND. (#7562)}\par
00029 {\cf20 //  2024-04-16: OpenGL: Detect ES3 contexts on desktop based on version string, to e.g. avoid calling glPolygonMode() on them. (#7447)}\par
00030 {\cf20 //  2024-01-09: OpenGL: Update GL3W based imgui_impl_opengl3_loader.h to load "libGL.so" and variants, fixing regression on distros missing a symlink.}\par
00031 {\cf20 //  2023-11-08: OpenGL: Update GL3W based imgui_impl_opengl3_loader.h to load "libGL.so" instead of "libGL.so.1", accommodating for NetBSD systems having only "libGL.so.3" available. (#6983)}\par
00032 {\cf20 //  2023-10-05: OpenGL: Rename symbols in our internal loader so that LTO compilation with another copy of gl3w is possible. (#6875, #6668, #4445)}\par
